From f2561d37add06623982d7b9719f172fa522fa316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/36] Add the ComfyUI workflow templates the Bench binds into

Seven API-format graphs: text to image with a LoRA stack and a guidance
chain, two-pass hires, regional prompting with up to four masked regions,
only-masked inpaint, Ultimate SD Upscale, a face/eyes/hands detail chain
and a three-deep ControlNet stack.

Each carries its own manifest: the node classes it cannot run without, the
typed inputs a recipe binds to (by node title first, node id second), and
the optional occurrences that are pruned out when a recipe does not use
them. Node ids are literal and never regenerated, because ComfyUI's
execution cache is keyed on them.

Every class name and input name was checked against ComfyUI's own node
definitions rather than written from memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmpuZqpQrFjas3Ajv22pKb
